{
  "A native `<button>` styled with design tokens. It comes in three variants, three tones and three sizes, and supports an icon and an `&` access key. A button can act as a toggle, indicate that work is in progress, and open a menu or any other content, either from the whole button or from an arrow next to it with `split`, so the button keeps its own action.": "",
  "Both approaches are fully supported. Every prop accepts a value or a function, and a function that reads a reactive object keeps the button in sync with it. Setting a property programmatically works the same way.": "",
  "Variants, tones and sizes": "",
  "`solid` buttons have an opaque fill, a bottom edge, a highlight along the top and a slight movement when pressed. `outline` buttons have a frame, and `ghost` buttons show a background only on hover. The tone sets the colors, and the size sets the height from the density tokens. Turn on Compact above to see the difference.": "",
  "Text, icons and children": "",
  "`text` sets the caption, and JSX children follow it. `icon` accepts an image address or any element or component, placed before or after the text with `iconPosition`. A button with only an icon needs an accessible name, so give it a `hint`.": "",
  "Toggle buttons": "",
  "With `toggle`, a click turns `pressed` on and off. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "Busy state": "",
  "While `busy` is set, a spinner appears over the content, clicks are ignored and the size does not change. The text remains available to screen readers, and the button gets `aria-busy`.": "",
  "Disabled state": "",
  "A disabled button uses the native disabled state, so it leaves the Tab order and cannot be pressed. With `focusableWhenDisabled`, it keeps its place in the Tab order and only gets `aria-disabled`. Keyboard and screen reader users can still reach it, and a hint can explain why it is unavailable.": "",
  "With `menu`, the whole button opens a list of commands. Items can have an icon, a check mark or a group separator, and can be disabled or hidden. While the menu is open, each `&` key selects its item. An item field can be a function, and the open menu tracks what it reads.": "",
  "Split button": "",
  "With `split`, the button keeps its own action (`onclick`) and an arrow next to it opens the menu. The two parts are separate Tab stops, and Alt+Down on the button also opens the menu. You can change `split` at any time, but the menu itself (`split`, `menu` or `dropDown`) must exist when the button is created, because it divides the button into two parts.": "",
  "`dropDown` opens any component instead of a menu, such as a picker or a small form. Focus moves to its first field, and Escape or a click outside closes it.": "",
  "Presses the button. With a menu and no `split`, it opens the menu and moves focus to the first item.": "",
  "Presses the button (Control + Option + key on Apple platforms).": "",
  "On a button that opens a menu, or on the arrow of a split button, opens the menu and moves focus to the first or last item.": "",
  "On the main part of a split button, opens the menu.": "",
  "Moves to the next or previous item, wrapping at the ends. Disabled items are reachable.": "",
  "Moves to the first or last item.": "",
  "Selects the item with that `&` key. Otherwise, focus moves to the next item that starts with that letter.": "",
  "Selects the focused item.": "",
  "Closes the menu or drop-down, and focus returns to the part that opened it.": "",
  "Closes the menu and moves to the next control.": "",
  "A native `<button>` (two with `split`: the button and the arrow), so forms, Enter, Space and screen readers work as expected.": "",
  "The text without the `&` marker. An icon-only button is named by its `hint` or by your `aria-label`. The arrow of a split button gets its name from `uiLocale` (\"More options\").": "",
  "`aria-busy=\"true\"`. The text remains readable under the spinner.": "",
  "`aria-haspopup=\"menu\"` and `aria-expanded` on the part that opens the menu. The list has `role=\"menu\"`, items are `menuitem` or `menuitemcheckbox` with `aria-checked`, disabled items have `aria-disabled`, and group separators are `separator`.": "",
  "`aria-haspopup=\"dialog\"`. The popup has `role=\"dialog\"` and is named by the button's text. Focus moves to its first field.": "",
  "Shown only during keyboard use, with the design system's double ring.": "",
  "The only string a button displays on its own is the name of a split button's arrow. It comes from `uiLocale.strings`, which starts from the page's `lang` (English and Turkish are included) and can be set to any `UiStrings`. Every button updates immediately. The set is used as provided, so to change one string, assign a new set: `uiLocale.strings = { ...uiLocale.strings, moreOptions: 'Mehr' }`. Changing a string inside the existing set has no effect.": "",
  "The button, or the group of a button with a menu. `data-variant`, `data-tone`, `data-size`, `data-icon-position`, `data-stretch`, `data-pressed`, `data-busy`, `data-icon`, `data-mode=\"menu|split\"`.": "",
  "The pressable part: the button itself, or `.mx-button__main` and `.mx-button__arrow`.": "",
  "The icon, the arrow glyph of a menu button and the busy spinner.": "",
  "The surface the menu opens on (`data-side=\"bottom|top\"`).": "Menünün üzerinde açıldığı yüzey (`data-side=\"bottom|top\"`).",
  "The menu, its items and its group separators.": "",
  "Unit: the pressable part, with its frame (the bottom side is the key edge), its fill and state layer (`image`) and its focus ring (outline and `glow`). Each appearance is a state (`accent`, `danger`, `outline`, `outline-accent`, `ghost`, …), and each appearance has its own states (`hover`, `toggled-hover`, `open`, `pressed`, `focus`, `toggled`, `disabled`: `outline-hover`, `accent-pressed`, …). There are also `icon-only`, `busy`, and the `main` and `arrow` parts of a split button.": "",
  "Units: the icon, the text, the menu arrow (`open`), the busy spinner and the split button divider. Each appearance is a state.": "",
  "The distance a solid button moves when pressed, the square icon button, the caption line box and the spinner rotation.": "",
  "The popup surface and the menu items.": "Popup yüzeyi ve menü öğeleri.",
  "All of these reference design system tokens (see [Tokens](/tokens)). Override one after `styles.css` to restyle every button.": "",
  "The caption. `&` marks the access key (`&Save` → Alt+S), and `&&` produces a literal `&`. JSX children follow it.": "",
  "`solid` (filled and pressable), `outline` (framed) or `ghost` (visible only on hover).": "",
  "`standard`, `accent` for the primary action, or `danger` for a destructive action.": "",
  "`sm`, `md` or `lg`, which map to the control heights in the density tokens.": "",
  "An image address, or any element or component (an `<svg>` in JSX, an icon font tag). It is decorative and hidden from screen readers.": "",
  "Places the icon before or after the text.": "",
  "The native type. The default is `button`, so a button inside a form never submits by accident.": "",
  "A tooltip (`title`). It also provides the name of an icon-only button.": "",
  "Makes it a toggle button. A click turns `pressed` on and off (`aria-pressed`).": "",
  "The state of a toggle button. `x-model` provides two-way binding.": "",
  "Indicates that work is in progress. A spinner appears over the content, clicks are ignored, the size is preserved and `aria-busy` is set.": "",
  "When disabled, the button stays in the Tab order with `aria-disabled`, so a screen reader can find it and announce it as dimmed.": "",
  "With a menu, the button keeps its own action and an arrow next to it opens the menu. Without `split`, the whole button opens the menu.": "",
  "The menu commands, read each time the menu opens.": "",
  "Any content to open instead of a menu, such as a picker or a small form.": "",
  "Set programmatically with a value or a function, the same as the prop: `b.tone = () => this.state.tone` is tracked, and `b.tone = 'accent'` replaces it.": "",
  "Maps to `pressed` for `x-model`.": "",
  "Indicates whether the menu or drop-down is open. Set it to open or close it.": "",
  "Indicates whether the button was created with `split`, `menu` or `dropDown`.": "",
  "Opens the menu or drop-down with focus on its first item. Returns `false` if there is nothing to open, or if the button is disabled or busy.": "",
  "Closes it. If focus is inside, it returns to the part that opened it.": "",
  "Your menu items can be plain or reactive, and the button reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. An open menu shows the change immediately.": "",
  "Sets focus on the button, or on its main part if it has a menu.": "",
  "The DOM click event of the button, which runs its own action. With `split`, the arrow and the menu do not raise it. With a menu and no `split`, the click opens the menu.": "",
  "Occurs when a menu item is selected, after the item's own `click`. `e`: `{ item, source, event }`.": "",
  "MenuItem": "MenuItem",
  "The label. `&` marks the key that selects it while the menu is open.": "",
  "An icon. A function is called each time the item is drawn.": "",
  "`false` shows the item dimmed. It stays reachable but cannot be selected.": "",
  "`false` removes the item.": "",
  "When set, the item is a `menuitemcheckbox` and shows a check mark when `true`. Change it in `click`.": "",
  "function": "fonksiyon",
  "Runs when the item is selected, after the menu closes.": "",
  "A custom application value.": "",
  "The menu and the surface it opens on are shared parts, `MenuList` and `Popup`, exported for use in other components.": ""
}
